(3770017, 533098, 9906, '<td valign="top">This photo has a lot of problems with it that come from (IMHO) a probable combination of three facters.  It looks like it was indoors in a very low lighting situation.  This makes your camera want to shoot at a higher ISO (causing more noise).  It looks like you were probably zoomed way out (causing loss of sharpness which you want to try and fix with sharpening).  It looks like a very tight crop (makes the noise in the shot even worse and makes it harder to correct colors and such because of the lower amount of data).  How do you take better shots in these situations?  Kinda depends on your camera.  Without that info I can''t give good suggestions but if you post this in the forums after the challenge is over I''m sure you can get a lot of info to help in the future.<br/>TC</td>', 'This photo has a lot of problems with it that come from (IMHO) a probable combination of three facters.  It looks like it was indoors in a very low lighting situation.  This makes your camera want to shoot at a higher ISO (causing more noise).  It looks like you were probably zoomed way out (causing loss of sharpness which you want to try and fix with sharpening).  It looks like a very tight crop (makes the noise in the shot even worse and makes it harder to correct colors and such because of the lower amount of data).  How do you take better shots in these situations?  Kinda depends on your camera.  Without that info I can''t give good suggestions but if you post this in the forums after the challenge is over I''m sure you can get a lot of info to help in the future.TC', '2007-06-11 21:03:00.000000', NULL, 1),
