(3779511, 532725, 72774, '<td valign="top">I like it, it''s got that late night ''moment in time'' feel which appeals to me.  My initial thought is 7 but I''ll see if that changes.<br/> <br/>There''s a bit of blurring in the subject which is a feature -- where it counts (his face, hand) it is sharp.  I wish his face was a little sharper, but this must have been a pretty long shutter and that would be hard.  I like that the secondary subject is very blurred, it is a really nice effect.<br/> <br/>I definitely like the desat in this case -- at night, our ability to see color diminishes so B&amp;W always seems right for nighttime shots to me.<br/> <br/>Composition is good, but I really wish his hand was not at the edge of the photo.  That hurts the photo a lot for me, especially in terms of the title.  It doesn''t help that his hand blew out a bit too -- I wish that was more featured.  But his face draws me in, and that''s the way it is supposed to be.  I like the border, didn''t even notice it at first, but it enhances the darkness idea.<br/> <br/>One final comment, more about the subject than the photo -- I''ve called the subject a man, but he has some feminine aspects (shirt, necklace, earring).  He has manly aspects too (arms, watch, hair, etc).  Is he transgender?  I think it adds a lot to the image, the non-obvious combination of male and female traits and adds a little mystery.<br/> <br/>So, I''ll stick to a 7.  The hand is the main flaw that keeps me from going higher (and the slight blurring of his face). <br/> <br/>------------<br/> <br/>This comment courtesy the <b>Viral Comment Experiment</b> (<b>VCE</b>).  The VCE is an experiment to see if a large number of quality comments can be generated in a fashion similar to chain letters.  The first time you receive a VCE comment, <b>randomly choose five (5) images</b> from this challenge (or another challenge) and leave quality, useful comments/critiques like this one.  Make sure to mention good things as we