(3781938, 531482, 44877, '<td valign="top">This is an interesting photo with a lot of atmosphere. Even though it is quite busy, the eye is drawn to your subject on the bottom left. Good job with that! <br/> <br/>The black and white conversion works well for this photo and it''s sad theme. <br/>Good contrasts and tones on the B&amp;W. <br/> <br/>The motion blur in some of the passers-by supports the focal point of the image.  Also that the heads are cut off is a smart way to support the topic. Overall very good composition. <br/> <br/>I feel the photo has too much noise - which might have been intended, but it bothers me. I take into consideration that this is an impromptu street shot, of course. <br/> <br/>The title is very distracting to me. I will take into consideration that English may not be your first language, in which case I would recommend keeping the titles short and check for spelling and punctuation. This is a very strong image that speaks for itself. The long title waters down the message that you captured so well. <br/> <br/>All of that said, I''m voting a 6 and feel it would deserve to finish in the low sixes. Good luck!<br/> <br/>**************************************************<br/> <br/> <br/>This comment courtesy the Viral Comment Experiment (VCE). The VCE is an experiment to see if a large number of quality comments can be generated in a fashion similar to chain letters. The first time you receive a VCE comment, randomly choose five (5) images from this challenge (or another challenge) and leave quality, useful comments/critiques like this one. Make sure to mention good things as well as bad things. Then, see how many you receive in return over the next few weeks. Make sure you copy this VCE notice at the end of each comment. [Obligatory chain letter threat] If you do not make five quality comments within 24 hours, your hard drive will crash and your camera''s shutter will fail at an inopportune moment.</td>', 'This is an interesting photo with a lot of atmosphere. Even though it is quite busy, the eye is drawn to your subject on the bottom left. Good job with that!  The black and white conversion works well for this photo and it''s sad theme. Good contrasts and tones on the B&W.  The motion blur in some of the passers-by supports the focal point of the image.  Also that the heads are cut off is a smart way to support the topic. Overall very good composition.  I feel the photo has too much noise - which might have been intended, but it bothers me. I take into consideration that this is an impromptu street shot, of course.  The title is very distracting to me. I will take into consideration that English may not be your first language, in which case I would recommend keeping the titles short and check for spelling and punctuation. This is a very strong image that speaks for itself. The long title waters down the message that you captured so well.  All of that said, I''m voting a 6 and feel it would deserve to finish in the low sixes. Good luck! **************************************************  This comment courtesy the Viral Comment Experiment (VCE). The VCE is an experiment to see if a large number of quality comments can be generated in a fashion similar to chain letters. The first time you receive a VCE comment, randomly choose five (5) images from this challenge (or another challenge) and leave quality, useful comments/critiques like this one. Make sure to mention good things as well as bad things. Then, see how many you receive in return over the next few weeks. Make sure you copy this VCE notice at the end of each comment. [Obligatory chain letter threat] If you do not make five quality comments within 24 hours, your hard drive will crash and your camera''s shutter will fail at an inopportune moment.', '2007-06-14 03:19:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(3781969, 532266, 44877, '<td valign="top">Avant guarde was the first word that popped into my head when I saw this image. From the thumb you can''t really tell what''s going on, but it is interesting enough to want to find out. <br/> <br/>In many ways this photo is brilliant - the circular design in conjunction with the motion blurred pedestrians gives a great swirling feeling. <br/> <br/>Your focal point - the man on the black animal bench - is perfectly positions per the rule of thirds. The colors are very pretty, crisp and clear. A feast for the eyes. <br/> <br/>I''m torn about the escalator on the bottom right. On the one hand it is visually interesting, but it is also distracting. I''ve held my hand over it to see how the photo would look without it and I find it would benefit from the absence of the escalator. However, I realize there was probably nothing you could do about it without cropping too drastically. <br/> <br/>The title is good and supports the message of the photo. Also handy in case someone doesn''t see the focal point of the image. <br/> <br/>That all said, I''m giving it an 8. Hope other voters appreciate the quirkiness of this excellent composition. <br/> <br/>************************************************************<br/> <br/>This comment courtesy the Viral Comment Experiment (VCE). The VCE is an experiment to see if a large number of quality comments can be generated in a fashion similar to chain letters. The first time you receive a VCE comment, randomly choose five (5) images from this challenge (or another challenge) and leave quality, useful comments/critiques like this one. Make sure to mention good things as well as bad things. Then, see how many you receive in return over the next few weeks. Make sure you copy this VCE notice at the end of each comment. [Obligatory chain letter threat] If you do not make five quality comments within 24 hours, your hard drive will crash and your camera''s shutter will fail at an inopportune moment.</td>', 'Avant guarde was the first word that popped into my head when I saw this image. From the thumb you can''t really tell what''s going on, but it is interesting enough to want to find out.  In many ways this photo is brilliant - the circular design in conjunction with the motion blurred pedestrians gives a great swirling feeling.  Your focal point - the man on the black animal bench - is perfectly positions per the rule of thirds. The colors are very pretty, crisp and clear. A feast for the eyes.  I''m torn about the escalator on the bottom right. On the one hand it is visually interesting, but it is also distracting. I''ve held my hand over it to see how the photo would look without it and I find it would benefit from the absence of the escalator. However, I realize there was probably nothing you could do about it without cropping too drastically.  The title is good and supports the message of the photo. Also handy in case someone doesn''t see the focal point of the image.  That all said, I''m giving it an 8. Hope other voters appreciate the quirkiness of this excellent composition.  ************************************************************ This comment courtesy the Viral Comment Experiment (VCE). The VCE is an experiment to see if a large number of quality comments can be generated in a fashion similar to chain letters. The first time you receive a VCE comment, randomly choose five (5) images from this challenge (or another challenge) and leave quality, useful comments/critiques like this one. Make sure to mention good things as well as bad things. Then, see how many you receive in return over the next few weeks. Make sure you copy this VCE notice at the end of each comment. [Obligatory chain letter threat] If you do not make five quality comments within 24 hours, your hard drive will crash and your camera''s shutter will fail at an inopportune moment.', '2007-06-14 03:31:40.000000', NULL, 1),
