(3793338, 533150, 36006, '<td valign="top">This has nothing to do with your photograph.<br/> <br/>STUPID FUCK!!!!<br/> <br/>Ok, now that I got that out of my system.<br/> <br/>Nice comp, tonal values are ok, the blacks seem a bit deep, nice texture, ok light, the thing in the bottom left corner is distracting, overall a nice candid.</td>', 'This has nothing to do with your photograph. STUPID FUCK!!!! Ok, now that I got that out of my system. Nice comp, tonal values are ok, the blacks seem a bit deep, nice texture, ok light, the thing in the bottom left corner is distracting, overall a nice candid.', '2007-06-17 09:50:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(3793351, 533121, 36006, '<td valign="top">I''ve got to ask myself, <br/> <br/>How is a sports action shot a candid shot? The athlete is not on the sidelines, or getting a drink, or standing in line at the concession stand, or getting out of his car, or signing an autograph.<br/> <br/>Sports action is just that, "action". A candid is something totally differant.<br/> <br/>Photgraphically speaking however, this is a great "action" shot.<br/> <br/>The tonal values are excellent, the light is great, great texture, great emotional value, excellent comp, excellent dof, the fence pole going up the athletes leg is not wanted, over all, this is not a candid scene, but a very good sports action scene.</td>', 'I''ve got to ask myself,  How is a sports action shot a candid shot? The athlete is not on the sidelines, or getting a drink, or standing in line at the concession stand, or getting out of his car, or signing an autograph. Sports action is just that, "action". A candid is something totally differant. Photgraphically speaking however, this is a great "action" shot. The tonal values are excellent, the light is great, great texture, great emotional value, excellent comp, excellent dof, the fence pole going up the athletes leg is not wanted, over all, this is not a candid scene, but a very good sports action scene.', '2007-06-17 09:56:27.000000', NULL, 1),
