(3800868, 530861, 8522, '<td valign="top">IMO, the point of DPC challenges is not to meet them to the letter, but to meet the spirit of the challenge. Photographing a family member in your car is not meeting the spirit of the challenge in my book. What did you learn with this shot? Did it take as much courage as photographing a stranger? Was it as hard to anticipate the expression as someone you''ve never met? And in this particular shot, what was so special about this expression that it had to be captured for posterity? Why would you have taken this shot if it wasn''t for a DPC challenge? Will it stand the test of time? It''s exactly the sense of context (the inside of a car) that makes this a poor shot for me. The reason for the shot has to have been stalking a kid or a family snapshot.</td>', 'IMO, the point of DPC challenges is not to meet them to the letter, but to meet the spirit of the challenge. Photographing a family member in your car is not meeting the spirit of the challenge in my book. What did you learn with this shot? Did it take as much courage as photographing a stranger? Was it as hard to anticipate the expression as someone you''ve never met? And in this particular shot, what was so special about this expression that it had to be captured for posterity? Why would you have taken this shot if it wasn''t for a DPC challenge? Will it stand the test of time? It''s exactly the sense of context (the inside of a car) that makes this a poor shot for me. The reason for the shot has to have been stalking a kid or a family snapshot.', '2007-06-19 08:49:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(3800874, 531846, 4411, '<td valign="top">This picture is haunting me now.<br/> <br/>Not because of Don''s comments :D - well actually it is one of his comments ... the mention of Hitchcock has for some reason set the theme tune to ''Tales of the Unexpected'' playing in my head. Even though that was in colour and nothing to do with Hitchcock!<br/> <br/>It was a fairground style tune though, and I guess that''s my brain just picking up a reference from my youth to match the retro atmosphere, and this photo has that in abundance.<br/> <br/>God I hope this makes sense. I came back intending to leave a better comment but I''m not sure I succeeded : )</td>', 'This picture is haunting me now. Not because of Don''s comments :D - well actually it is one of his comments ... the mention of Hitchcock has for some reason set the theme tune to ''Tales of the Unexpected'' playing in my head. Even though that was in colour and nothing to do with Hitchcock! It was a fairground style tune though, and I guess that''s my brain just picking up a reference from my youth to match the retro atmosphere, and this photo has that in abundance. God I hope this makes sense. I came back intending to leave a better comment but I''m not sure I succeeded : )', '2007-06-19 08:57:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(3800928, 531228, 66597, '<td valign="top">This is a beautiful photo! Many congrats on your well-deserved ribbon!</td>', 'This is a beautiful photo! Many congrats on your well-deserved ribbon!', '2007-06-19 09:25:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3800940, 531867, 35357, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jbsmithana:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice shot.  BTW - I think you have your lenses mixed up. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>You''re right.  I fixed it, thanks!</td>', 'Originally posted by jbsmithana: Nice shot.  BTW - I think you have your lenses mixed up.  You''re right.  I fixed it, thanks!', '2007-06-19 09:33:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(3800997, 531846, 30982, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bod:</b></div><hr/><i> This picture is haunting me now.<br/> <br/>Not because of Don''s comments :D - well actually it is one of his comments ... the mention of Hitchcock has for some reason set the theme tune to ''Tales of the Unexpected'' playing in my head. Even though that was in colour and nothing to do with Hitchcock!<br/> <br/>It was a fairground style tune though, and I guess that''s my brain just picking up a reference from my youth to match the retro atmosphere, and this photo has that in abundance.<br/> <br/>God I hope this makes sense. I came back intending to leave a better comment but I''m not sure I succeeded : ) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I do think you succeeded.  The fact that the picture has brought about differing opinions, references, and strangely, Hitchcockian inferences, means that it''s more than just a nice snapshot.  It''s always interesting to me how different people interpret the same thing, and I''m pleased the "retro" aspect came through, despite the tread on her shoes.  And for the record, yours was the one I saw in the challenge that made me say "Gosh, I thought mine was pretty good, but this is better!" for the sheer emotion of it.  And I didn''t realize these shots were cliche, but I really don''t get out much.  :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by bod: This picture is haunting me now. Not because of Don''s comments :D - well actually it is one of his comments ... the mention of Hitchcock has for some reason set the theme tune to ''Tales of the Unexpected'' playing in my head. Even though that was in colour and nothing to do with Hitchcock! It was a fairground style tune though, and I guess that''s my brain just picking up a reference from my youth to match the retro atmosphere, and this photo has that in abundance. God I hope this makes sense. I came back intending to leave a better comment but I''m not sure I succeeded : )   I do think you succeeded.  The fact that the picture has brought about differing opinions, references, and strangely, Hitchcockian inferences, means that it''s more than just a nice snapshot.  It''s always interesting to me how different people interpret the same thing, and I''m pleased the "retro" aspect came through, despite the tread on her shoes.  And for the record, yours was the one I saw in the challenge that made me say "Gosh, I thought mine was pretty good, but this is better!" for the sheer emotion of it.  And I didn''t realize these shots were cliche, but I really don''t get out much.  :-)', '2007-06-19 09:57:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3801282, 531898, 30982, '<td valign="top">OK, sue me for paying attention to the picture and not the details - just noticed your title.  You should shoot people more often - it really is kinda fun!  (And very smart move to include the DPC-mandated water droplets, I might add...)  :-)</td>', 'OK, sue me for paying attention to the picture and not the details - just noticed your title.  You should shoot people more often - it really is kinda fun!  (And very smart move to include the DPC-mandated water droplets, I might add...)  :-)', '2007-06-19 11:18:58.000000', NULL, 0),
