(3854690, 532740, 79604, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by BeckyT:</b></div><hr/><i> Very nice shot of the dragonfly.  Focus is nice and crisp.  A boost in saturation I think would help this dragonfly pop. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Lovely photo and a beautiful macro. I agree with Becky...a bit more saturation might work well.</td>', 'Originally posted by BeckyT: Very nice shot of the dragonfly.  Focus is nice and crisp.  A boost in saturation I think would help this dragonfly pop.   Lovely photo and a beautiful macro. I agree with Becky...a bit more saturation might work well.', '2007-07-01 19:49:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(3859520, 531228, 27763, '<td valign="top">I remember this one from the recent Candid challenge.  This is an excellent capture.  And it doesn''t bother me at all that you can''t see their faces.  I prefer it this way.  It''s kind of like they''re "riding off into the sunset" at the end of a long, hard day.<br/>Congratulations on your ribbon!</td>', 'I remember this one from the recent Candid challenge.  This is an excellent capture.  And it doesn''t bother me at all that you can''t see their faces.  I prefer it this way.  It''s kind of like they''re "riding off into the sunset" at the end of a long, hard day.Congratulations on your ribbon!', '2007-07-02 18:16:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(3861050, 531334, 43298, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the honourable mention. In my opinion it is very hard to get a candid shot that is actually a decent photo, and this one is great :)</td>', 'Congrats on the honourable mention. In my opinion it is very hard to get a candid shot that is actually a decent photo, and this one is great :)', '2007-07-02 23:47:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(3873739, 529747, 31637, '<td valign="top">Where''d ya find this guy? I need more candids of homeless photography, or characters like this.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-07-05 21:32:52.</i></td>', 'Where''d ya find this guy? I need more candids of homeless photography, or characters like this.', '2007-07-05 22:32:09.000000', '2007-07-05 22:32:52.000000', 0),
(3878258, 532599, 48389, '<td valign="top">Really interesting shot! Fits the challenge nicely. I am wondering what this would have looked like in landscape orientation and with more of the jetty included? :o)</td>', 'Really interesting shot! Fits the challenge nicely. I am wondering what this would have looked like in landscape orientation and with more of the jetty included? :o)', '2007-07-07 13:02:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(3888239, 531857, 35720, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ambaker:</b></div><hr/><i> Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>Except for the hair style, this could be an 80 year old picture.<br/> <br/>Depth of field is used well to set the subject apart from the rest of the image.  Though I might have preferred even a bit shallower depth of field.  <br/> <br/>Lighting is very good for this piece, and a very good job of capturing a "far away" look in the subject''s eyes.<br/> <br/>Good job of not letting the whites get blown out, or the contrast too shallow.<br/> <br/>A good photo tells a story, and this one tells a story of a young lady whose mind is elsewhere.  <br/> <br/>Good job. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Many thanks for a good critique Alex, it''s much appreciated.</td>', 'Originally posted by ambaker: Critique Club Review: Except for the hair style, this could be an 80 year old picture. Depth of field is used well to set the subject apart from the rest of the image.  Though I might have preferred even a bit shallower depth of field.   Lighting is very good for this piece, and a very good job of capturing a "far away" look in the subject''s eyes. Good job of not letting the whites get blown out, or the contrast too shallow. A good photo tells a story, and this one tells a story of a young lady whose mind is elsewhere.   Good job.   Many thanks for a good critique Alex, it''s much appreciated.', '2007-07-10 07:22:02.000000', NULL, 0);
