(3902918, 532740, 28742, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by annig:</b></div><hr/><i>POST CHALLENGE: GEE! WHAT A BUNCH OF CRANKS VOTED IN THIS CHALLENGE.. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>LOL - don''t let them get ya down. With an occasional, enjoyable exception, you either shoot for the voters/scores or you shoot for yourself, but do not confuse the two. ;-)</td>', 'Originally posted by annig:POST CHALLENGE: GEE! WHAT A BUNCH OF CRANKS VOTED IN THIS CHALLENGE..  LOL - don''t let them get ya down. With an occasional, enjoyable exception, you either shoot for the voters/scores or you shoot for yourself, but do not confuse the two. ;-)', '2007-07-14 13:35:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(3913949, 532518, 48587, '<td valign="top">i don''t get it.</td>', 'i don''t get it.', '2007-07-18 10:48:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(3922387, 532973, 51538, '<td valign="top">I like coming back long after a challenge has finished to enjoy the images for what they''re worth outside the confines of the rules.  It''s interesting how different some photos appear when one is not having to vote them up or down.  For instance, this quiet sample of non-urban life sticks in my mind.  It has a persistence.  In my own collection of photos, it is images like this which remind me of moments in time and they are valuable to me.  Nice work - as is much in your folio...</td>', 'I like coming back long after a challenge has finished to enjoy the images for what they''re worth outside the confines of the rules.  It''s interesting how different some photos appear when one is not having to vote them up or down.  For instance, this quiet sample of non-urban life sticks in my mind.  It has a persistence.  In my own collection of photos, it is images like this which remind me of moments in time and they are valuable to me.  Nice work - as is much in your folio...', '2007-07-20 17:25:27.000000', NULL, 0),
