(3941788, 531678, 31403, '<td valign="top">hurting their eyes is good for them - :-)  <br/> <br/>I love it!<br/> <br/>I shot a chair for a still life or some such challenge with a lens baby - I love the shot still, but alack - I hurt their eyes!  :-)  LOL<br/> <br/><a href="//flickr.com/photos/digitalknight/641836938/in/set-72157600772551577/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//flickr.com/photos/digitalknight/641836938/in/set-72157600772551577/</a></td>', 'hurting their eyes is good for them - :-)   I love it! I shot a chair for a still life or some such challenge with a lens baby - I love the shot still, but alack - I hurt their eyes!  :-)  LOL //flickr.com/photos/digitalknight/641836938/in/set-72157600772551577/', '2007-07-27 03:00:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3942496, 532898, 62318, '<td valign="top">Good color rendition. Interesting pose, though I wish there was a bit more context at what he is looking at. Good choice for Candid.</td>', 'Good color rendition. Interesting pose, though I wish there was a bit more context at what he is looking at. Good choice for Candid.', '2007-07-27 11:15:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(3947329, 531925, 81803, '<td valign="top">Hi....i''m not quite sure what you did, but if i sat here a bit longer &amp; really gave it a little thought-- anyway, you have some "bleedover" from the sky onto your subject, presumably in the places you cloned out distractions (such as the powerlines), and maybe from your application of the sky filter.<br/> <br/>I read what someone else said about the exposure on the subject. i agree, you might have done a *leeetle* touch of selective exposure adjustment, but overall, it''sa  good capture, a good candid.<br/> <br/>As an amateur myself, and still trying to convince the paper that they ought to hire me rather than hope they can get any more"freebies" outta me (now I just show ''em what I got, tell them the story, and if they don''t care to pay me for it, as a freelancer, i politely thank them and go away. Hopefully one of these days, they''ll see another they just can''t live without!) (-:  Maybe I''ll get assignments someday if i keep rooting out stories on my own!<br/> <br/>My camera goes everywhere with me; you just never know what''s around the next bend, literally! Good job, keep up the good work, and congrats on the assignment!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-07-29 21:01:30.</i></td>', 'Hi....i''m not quite sure what you did, but if i sat here a bit longer & really gave it a little thought-- anyway, you have some "bleedover" from the sky onto your subject, presumably in the places you cloned out distractions (such as the powerlines), and maybe from your application of the sky filter. I read what someone else said about the exposure on the subject. i agree, you might have done a *leeetle* touch of selective exposure adjustment, but overall, it''sa  good capture, a good candid. As an amateur myself, and still trying to convince the paper that they ought to hire me rather than hope they can get any more"freebies" outta me (now I just show ''em what I got, tell them the story, and if they don''t care to pay me for it, as a freelancer, i politely thank them and go away. Hopefully one of these days, they''ll see another they just can''t live without!) (-:  Maybe I''ll get assignments someday if i keep rooting out stories on my own! My camera goes everywhere with me; you just never know what''s around the next bend, literally! Good job, keep up the good work, and congrats on the assignment!', '2007-07-29 22:00:09.000000', '2007-07-29 22:01:30.000000', 0),
